==English==

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|en}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-set aside.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|set<,,set> aside}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[separate]] and [[reserve]] something for a specific [[purpose]].
#: {{ux|en|Plan to '''set aside''' three or four hours to see the museum.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[leave out]] of account; to [[omit]] or [[neglect]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1663<!-- possibly 20 March 1663 -->
|author=w:John Tillotson
|title=The Wisdom of Being Religious
|year2=1696
|chapter2=Sermon I
|title2=The Works of the Most Reverend Dr. John Tillotson
|location2=London|publisher2=B. Aylmer
|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=sOJBAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA31
|page2=31
|passage={{...}} therefore '''setting aside''' all other considerations, I will endeavour to know the truth, and yield to that.
}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[disagree]] with something and [[reject]] or [[overturn]] it.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To declare something [[invalid]] or [[null and void]].

